@startuml
' Figure 2.2 - Flow Chart, Existing Manual Workflow
'
' The process the proposed system replaces: order taken on a paper pad, a handwritten
' KOT carried to the kitchen, bills computed by hand, stock reconciled only at the end
' of the day. Same swimlanes and plain notation as Figure 3.7 so the two can be read
' against each other - the contrast between them is the argument for the system.
'
' The measured weaknesses from Section 1.2 are folded into the node labels rather than
' hung off the side as notes. A first draft used eight "note right" blocks; each one
' widens its lane, which took the canvas to 2484x2159 - aspect 1.15, printing the
' labels at 3.5pt. Width is the binding constraint on a four-lane diagram, so anything
' that widens a lane has to earn it.
'
' Figures carried across from Section 1.2 unchanged: 2-5 minutes per ticket,
' 5-15 percent monthly stock divergence, 2-3 percent arithmetic error rate per shift.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Arial"
skinparam defaultFontSize 21
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam ArrowColor #000000

skinparam activity {
  FontSize 21
  BorderThickness 1.6
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #000000
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  DiamondBorderColor #000000
  DiamondFontSize 20
  StartColor #000000
  EndColor #000000
}
skinparam swimlane {
  BorderColor #000000
  BorderThickness 1.6
  TitleFontSize 23
  TitleFontStyle bold
}
skinparam note {
  FontSize 19
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #000000
  BorderThickness 1.2
}

title
Flow Chart — Existing Manual Workflow
<size:10> </size>
end title

|Waiter|
start
:Seat customer, take order
on a paper pad;
:Handwrite kitchen order ticket,
keep the carbon copy;
:Carry ticket to the pass —
2 to 5 minutes per ticket;

|Kitchen|
:Spike ticket on the rail,
prepare in rail order;
if (Ingredient in stock?) then (no)
  :Tell the waiter, strike
  the dish off — nothing
  is recorded;
else (yes)
endif
:Call out when plated —
no reliable signal
reaches the waiter;

|Waiter|
:Notice the call,
collect and serve;

|Cashier|
:Find the carbon copy, add
line totals on a calculator;
:Work out service charge
and VAT by hand — 2 to 3
percent of bills are wrong;
if (Discount requested?) then (yes)
  :Apply at the cashier's
  discretion — no record of
  who authorised it;
else (no)
endif
:Take payment, write the receipt;
if (Void or refund?) then (yes)
  :Write a paper note —
  the only trace, easily
  lost or altered;
else (no)
endif

|Manager (end of day)|
:Gather tickets and receipts,
tally sales by hand;
:Count physical stock on the shelf;
if (Matches expected?) then (no)
  :Record the shortfall —
  stock diverges 5 to 15
  percent each month,
  loss unattributable;
else (yes)
endif
:Judge reorder quantities
from memory — no trigger,
no view of profitability
or demand;
stop

@enduml
